<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Proposal 38 GATE 5c, AC 19. THE WHOLE CHAIN, INSIDE THE APP, FOR THE FIRST
  TIME: PROPFIND -> GET -> cache -> project copy -> add-sample -> A CLIP THAT
  SOUNDS.

  Every piece of this existed and was gated in isolation before today. Gate 3
  drove the deferred `media:` branch against SDelayedLocalSource, a test-only
  provider that copies a LOCAL file after a delay - "the deferred BRANCH is what
  is under test, never the physics of a download", as its own header says. Gate 4
  drove SWebDavClient against the stub from a unit-test binary and had no app in
  it at all. This case is the join: the bytes the clip plays came out of a TCP
  socket.

  WHAT MAKES THAT ASSERTABLE. The stub serves the committed fixture tree with
  REAL FILE BYTES (fixtureDir="../media/lib"), and lib/kick.wav is a byte copy of
  ../test_sawtooth.wav - the RAMPED sawtooth whose per-source-second energy is a
  documented constant (testkit CONTRACT inv. 3). So the four assert-audio-energy
  windows below are the SAME numbers media_browser_drag_local.qxa asserts over
  the LOCAL provider, shifted by the same 48000 the drop asked for. A drop that
  placed the wrong file, at the wrong frame, or a truncated download, fails them.
  Asserting only that a clip exists would pass on every one of those.

  HOW THIS CASE LEARNS THE PORT: it does not. See media_webdav_browse.qxa's
  header - `media-webdav-stub` writes the stub's own baseUrl() into the account
  itself, because a .qxa cannot interpolate a run-time value and a FIXED port is
  exactly what makes concurrent cases collide.

  THE CACHE IS PER CASE. The CTest entry sets SMARAGD_MEDIA_CACHE_DIR into this
  case's own test-output directory, for the reason SMARAGD_SIDECAR_DIR exists:
  the cache is otherwise a shared per-user directory and `ctest -j4` runs four
  processes against it. Without it this case would write into the developer's
  real cache and its second-drop claim (below) would be measuring a hit inherited
  from a previous run.

  WHAT IT PINS

  1. The full chain, once. One drop of a REMOTE file, deferred, and when it lands
     there is exactly one clip at exactly 48000 - and it SOUNDS like the fixture,
     in the right place, with silence before it.
  2. THE PROJECT COPY (§B.6, T11). The project is SAVED BEFORE the drop, so the
     fetched file is copied to <projectdir>/media/ and the re-saved .qxp stores a
     RELATIVE path. A clip left pointing into the machine-local cache would
     serialise as an absolute path that means nothing on the next machine, which
     is the whole of what SFilePathRef exists to prevent. (The unsaved-project
     half - the warning, and the clip referencing the cache - is gate 3's
     media_drop_deferred; it is not repeated here.)
  3. A REPEAT DROP OF THE SAME REMOTE FILE REUSES BOTH CACHES. The second drop
     places SYNCHRONOUSLY (the assertion is made BEFORE media-drop-wait runs at
     all, so a second fetch would fail it), and the project copy is REUSED rather
     than disambiguated - "media/kick (2).wav" is asserted ABSENT. A user
     dragging the same loop onto four tracks gets one file.
  4. ONE UNDO STEP PER DROP. The placement is the same SAddSampleAction the
     `file:` branch has always submitted; there is no new action type anywhere in
     the media layer.

  WHAT IS NOT PINNED HERE

   * THE STUB IS NOT A NEXTCLOUD SERVER: plain HTTP, no TLS, no redirects, no
     rate limiting, no WWW-Authenticate challenge and NO REAL AUTHENTICATION (it
     never inspects the Authorization header it is sent), one canonical PROPFIND
     dialect. A real server is the manual runbook's job (§C.6 / gate 6).
   * A download big or slow enough to be interesting. 768 KB over loopback is not
     a network; fetchProgress, a mid-body close and a cancelled GET are gate 4's
     unit test, against this same stub.
   * The undo asymmetry (§B.6): undoing a deferred drop removes the clip and
     LEAVES THE COPIED FILE BEHIND, deliberately - the copy is not part of
     SAddSampleAction. Documented, not asserted.

  SETTINGS OWNERSHIP (trap T6). RUN_SERIAL. This case OWNS media/lastSourceId,
  media/lastPath/nextcloud:qxastub, media/categoryMask, media/searchRecursive and
  every key under media/nextcloud/qxastub/*; it restores the first four to their
  SOpt defaults and removes the account, so smaragd.ini comes back with identical
  CONTENT run to run. (CONTENT, not md5: QSettings rewrites the file from its own
  in-memory map and does not promise to preserve section ORDER across processes,
  so an md5 can legitimately move while every key is exactly as it was.)
  SMARAGD_SECRET_BACKEND=memory is set explicitly rather than inherited: the
  account only has to work for THIS process, and `memory` writes no INI key and
  no keychain item at all.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="media_webdav_drop">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <remove-media-account accountId="qxastub"/>

    <add-track index="-1"/>

    <!-- The project is saved FIRST so the fetched file has somewhere portable
         to be copied to (2). -->
    <save-project path="../../build/test-output/media_webdav_drop/media_webdav_drop.qxp"/>

    <media-webdav-stub accountId="qxastub" fixtureDir="../media/lib"
                       user="qxauser" password="qxapass" remember="0"/>

    <media-browser-filter categories="audio"/>
    <media-browser-source sourceId="nextcloud:qxastub" waitMs="10000"/>
    <assert-media-browser mode="browse" rowCount="3"
                          contains="kick.wav,768044,0"/>

    <!-- (1) The drop. The row reports NeedsFetch, so the panel builds a
         "media:<uri>" payload and the arranger's deferred branch takes it. -->
    <media-browser-drag name="kick.wav" trackPath="0" timePos="48000"/>
    <media-drop-wait waitMs="30000" placed="1" failed="0" abandoned="0"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,0" startTime="48000" duration="192000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,1" expectReject="true"/>

    <!-- ...and it SOUNDS like the fixture, in the right place. These are
         media_browser_drag_local.qxa's numbers, over the same audio, arrived at
         over a socket instead of off the disk. -->
    <render filename="drop.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="6"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="drop.wav"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="48000"
                         minRms="0" maxRms="0.002"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="drop.wav"
                         startFrame="48000" frameCount="48000"
                         minRms="0.05" maxRms="0.085"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="drop.wav"
                         startFrame="144000" frameCount="48000"
                         minRms="0.26" maxRms="0.33"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="drop.wav"
                         startFrame="192000" frameCount="48000"
                         minRms="0.37" maxRms="0.44"/>

    <!-- (2) The project copy, and the PORTABLE spelling it exists for. -->
    <save-project path="../../build/test-output/media_webdav_drop/media_webdav_drop.qxp"/>
    <assert-file-contains path="../../build/test-output/media_webdav_drop/media_webdav_drop.qxp"
                          text="media/kick.wav"/>

    <!-- (3) A repeat drop of the SAME remote file. Cached, so it places
         SYNCHRONOUSLY - asserted before media-drop-wait, which a second fetch
         would fail - and reuses the project copy rather than making a (2). -->
    <media-browser-drag name="kick.wav" trackPath="0" timePos="288000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,1" startTime="288000" duration="192000"/>
    <media-drop-wait waitMs="10000" placed="2" failed="0" abandoned="0"/>
    <save-project path="../../build/test-output/media_webdav_drop/media_webdav_drop.qxp"/>
    <assert-file-contains path="../../build/test-output/media_webdav_drop/media_webdav_drop.qxp"
                          text="media/kick (2).wav" absent="true"/>

    <!-- (4) One undo step per drop. -->
    <undo count="2"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,0" expectReject="true"/>

    <media-webdav-stub action="stop"/>

    <!-- Restore every key this case owns (T6). -->
    <remove-media-account accountId="qxastub"/>
    <assert-settings-file absent="nextcloud\qxastub\"/>
    <set-option key="media/lastSourceId" value="local"/>
    <set-option key="media/lastPath/nextcloud:qxastub" value=""/>
    <set-option key="media/categoryMask" value="1"/>
    <set-option key="media/searchRecursive" value="false"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="1"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
